		endpointName: 'searchContacts',
		label: 'Search contacts',
		description: "Returns the authenticated user's contacts that match a search query.",
		context:
			"---\nname: searchContacts\ndescription: Returns the authenticated user's contacts that match a search query.\n---\n\nSearches the grouped contacts of the authenticated user. The query matches prefix phrases on a\ncontact's names, nicknames, e-mail addresses, phone numbers and organizations from the contact source.\n\nImportant: Search uses a lazy cache that is updated after a request. Clients should first send a \nwarmup search request with an empty query to make sure the cache has the latest data.\n\nThis method has no page token: the result set is limited by the page size (at most 30).\n\nSee the [people.searchContacts reference](https://developers.google.com/people/api/rest/v1/people/searchContacts).",
		accounts: { google: { scope: ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/contacts.readonly'] } },
		annotations: {
			readOnlyHint: true,
			destructiveHint: false,
			idempotentHint: true,
			openWorldHint: false,
			arbitraryCallHint: false,
		},
